  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Seat Sherpa ("we", "us", or "our") operates the Seat Sherpa mobile application
    (the "App"), a peer-to-peer carpooling service available in California and Nevada.
    This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and
    your rights regarding that information.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information</strong> — name, email address, date of birth, profile photo.</li>
    <li><strong>Phone number</strong> — collected during signup and verified via SMS one-time code. Used to enable in-app voice communication between matched drivers and passengers.</li>
    <li><strong>Driver-only information</strong> — driver's license image and extracted name/date of birth, vehicle details (make, model, year, color, license plate, VIN), insurance card image, vehicle photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Ride information</strong> — origin and destination addresses, departure date/time, seat selection, messages exchanged in ride chats.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment information</strong> — collected and processed by Stripe Inc.; we do not store full card details on our servers.</li>
    <li><strong>Device information</strong> — push notification token, app version, operating system, anonymized usage events.</li>
    <li><strong>Location information</strong> — with your permission, we collect device location to help set pickup and drop-off points, find nearby rides, and understand where our service is used (aggregate demand analytics). You can grant or revoke location access at any time in your device settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create and manage your account.</li>
    <li>To verify your identity and prevent fraud (SMS phone verification, driver's license review).</li>
    <li>To match drivers with passengers, coordinate rides, and process payments.</li>
    <li>To send transactional notifications (booking confirmations, ride reminders, message alerts).</li>
    <li>To respond to support inquiries.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>To keep the community safe</strong> — authorized Seat Sherpa personnel may review
      in-app messages, reviews, and profile content in response to user reports, or where we
      reasonably suspect a violation of our Terms of Service (for example harassment, threats,
      fraud, or other safety concerns). Message content is never used for marketing or shared
      with third parties, and access is limited to trained staff acting on a safety or
      enforcement need.
    </li>
    <li>To comply with applicable legal obligations (e.g., 1099 reporting for drivers via Stripe Connect, identity-verification record-keeping).</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>We do not use your information for marketing purposes.</strong> We do not sell your data to third parties.</p>

  <h2>3. SMS messaging consent</h2>
  <p>
    During account creation, you provide your phone number and affirmatively consent
    to receive a one-time verification code via SMS by tapping "Send code." You may
    also receive transactional SMS reminders for upcoming rides. Standard SMS rates
    from your carrier may apply. You can opt out of further SMS at any time by
    replying STOP to any message. To re-opt-in, reply START. For help, reply HELP
    or email <a href="mailto:support@seatsherpa.app">support@seatsherpa.app</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not share SMS-related consent, phone numbers, or message content
    with third parties for marketing or promotional purposes.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>4. Service providers</h2>
  <p>We use the following service providers to operate the App:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — account database, authentication, file storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing and driver payouts (Stripe Connect).</li>
    <li><strong>Twilio</strong> — SMS verification code delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong> and <strong>Google</strong> — optional sign-in providers, push notification delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> — crash and error reporting. Crash reports include your account id and email address so we can identify and fix problems you actually hit.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each provider processes data only as required to deliver their service to us
    and is bound by their own privacy policies and data-processing agreements.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies, advertising &amp; analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Our website (seatsherpa.app) uses advertising pixels and analytics tags: the
    Meta Pixel, the Reddit Pixel, and the Google Ads tag, plus Vercel Analytics
    for aggregate page statistics. These tools set cookies or similar
    identifiers and receive information about your visit &mdash; pages viewed,
    device information, approximate location, and ad-click identifiers (such as
    <code>fbclid</code> or <code>rdt_cid</code>) &mdash; so we can measure our
    advertising and reach people who may be interested in Seat Sherpa. We also
    record ad-click identifiers in our own campaign statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (as amended by the CPRA), sending
    this information to advertising platforms may be considered
    &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; personal information for cross-context behavioral
    advertising. We do not sell personal information for money, and we do not
    knowingly share personal information of consumers under 16.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your opt-out choices.</strong> Our website honors the
    <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org" rel="noopener">Global Privacy
    Control</a> (GPC) browser signal: when your browser sends GPC, our
    advertising pixels are not loaded during your visit. You can also opt out
    with the platforms directly (Meta Ad Preferences, Reddit ad settings,
    Google My Ad Center), or email
    <a href="mailto:support@seatsherpa.app">support@seatsherpa.app</a> with the
    subject &ldquo;Do not share&rdquo; and we will honor your request. The App
    itself does not currently include third-party advertising SDKs.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Information sharing between users</h2>
  <p>
    To coordinate rides, your name, profile photo, ratings, and (after booking
    confirmation) phone number are shared with the matched driver or passenger.
    Phone calls placed through the App use your device's native dialer and the
    other party's phone number is visible to you. Drivers' vehicle details
    (make, model, color) are visible to passengers who book a seat; the license
    plate is revealed 2 hours before pickup. We do not share your information
    with users you have not been matched with.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Public ride listings.</strong> Posting a ride publishes limited
    listing information beyond the App so riders can find it: your first name,
    driver rating, route (departure and arrival areas and any listed stops),
    date and time, seat availability, and price. These fields appear on our
    public website (including seatsherpa.app/rides and route pages) and in
    third-party surfaces that list available rides, such as Apple Maps. Your
    contact details, exact addresses, license plate, and profile photo are not
    included in public listings.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your account information for as long as your account is active.
    You can delete your account at any time from within the app
    (Profile &rarr; Delete account) or by emailing
    <a href="mailto:support@seatsherpa.app">support@seatsherpa.app</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you delete your account, we erase your personal information &mdash;
    such as your name, profile photo, email address, phone number, and driver's
    license details &mdash; and permanently disable your login. Booking and trip
    records you created with other users are retained in an
    <strong>anonymized</strong> form (your name is replaced with
    &ldquo;Former member&rdquo;) so the other party keeps their own records and
    to meet tax, accounting, safety, and other legal obligations &mdash;
    generally for up to seven years.
  </p>
  <p>
    After deletion we retain a minimal deletion record &mdash; your account id,
    the email address on the account, and any reason you chose to give &mdash;
    for fraud prevention, audit, and legal-compliance purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your in-app message threads are handled differently: when you delete your
    account, the other party is notified that you have left, and the
    conversation is removed within a few days.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete,
    or port your personal information. California residents have specific rights
    under the CCPA, including the right to know what we collect and the right to
    request deletion. California residents may also opt out of the
    &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; of personal information for cross-context behavioral
    advertising as described in Section 5 &mdash; via the GPC browser signal or
    by emailing us. To exercise any of these rights, email
    <a href="mailto:support@seatsherpa.app">support@seatsherpa.app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use industry-standard security practices including encryption in transit
    (TLS), encryption at rest, role-based access controls, and regular security
    review. No system is perfectly secure; if you believe your account has been
    compromised, contact support immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Seat Sherpa is not directed to children under 18. All users must be 18 or
    older; drivers must also hold a current, valid driver's license. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Policy as the App evolves or as regulations change. Material
    changes will be communicated through the App or via email. The "Last updated"
    date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or concerns? Email
    <a href="mailto:support@seatsherpa.app">support@seatsherpa.app</a>.
  </p>

